-- title:
--   Essentially étale local algebras over A[T] at (varpi,T) are regular
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring which is a domain, a discrete valuation ring and a henselian local ring, and let $\varpi \in A$ be an element generating the maximal ideal, $\mathfrak m_A = (\varpi)$. Let $S$ be a commutative local domain and let $\varphi : A[X] \to S$ be a ring homomorphism which is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type. Assume given a ring homomorphism $\chi_0 : S \to A/\mathfrak m_A$ onto the residue field of $A$ whose kernel is exactly $\mathfrak m_S$, which induces the residue map on constants, i.e. $\chi_0(\varphi(C\,a)) = \bar a$ for all $a \in A$, and which kills the image of the variable, $\chi_0(\varphi(X)) = 0$. The conclusion is fourfold: $S$ is a regular local ring; its Krull dimension satisfies $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} S \le 2$; the maximal ideal of $S$ is generated by the two elements $\varphi(C\,\varpi)$ and $\varphi(X)$; and $\varphi(C\,\varpi)$ is a prime element of $S$.
--
--   This is the local algebra input for the study of a smooth point of a curve over a henselian discrete valuation ring: the hypotheses say that $S$ is an essentially étale local $A[T]$-algebra whose closed point is the residue-field rational point $(\varpi, T)$, and the conclusion identifies $S$ as a two-dimensional regular local ring with regular system of parameters $(\varpi, t)$ in which $\varpi$ stays prime. It is used in the construction of the algebraic block around a smooth point stalk, [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.smoothPointStalk_algebraicBlock_of_formallyEtale_of_henselian`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.smoothPointStalk_algebraicBlock_of_formallyEtale_of_henselian).
